%% Pudel DPoP (RFC 9449) Flow v2.5.0 (server-minted, BFF style)
%% The browser never signs a proof and never sees a key. Every authenticated
%% request gets a fresh, single-use, EdDSA proof minted and validated in-process.

sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as Vue Frontend
    participant Filter as JwtAuthenticationFilter
    participant Cookie as SessionCookieService
    participant KeyMgr as DPoPKeyManager
    participant DB as PostgreSQL (dpop_keys)
    participant DPoP as DPoPService

    Note over Client,DB: Step 1: Key material lives server-side only

    Client->>Filter: GET /api/guilds/{guildId}/settings (cookie only)
    Filter->>Cookie: readKeyId(request)
    Cookie-->>Filter: keyId (AES-GCM decrypted)
    Filter->>KeyMgr: findActiveSession(keyId)
    KeyMgr->>DB: SELECT public_key_jwk, private_key_jwk,<br/>public_key_thumbprint, access_token<br/>WHERE key_id=? AND is_active AND expires_at>now()
    DB-->>KeyMgr: DPoPKey row
    Note right of KeyMgr: OKP / crv=Ed25519 keypair.<br/>private_key_jwk never leaves the server.

    Note over Client,DB: Step 2: BFF mints the request-bound proof

    Filter->>KeyMgr: signInternalProof(keyId, method, uri, accessToken)
    KeyMgr->>KeyMgr: payload = { jti: UUID.randomUUID(),<br/>htm: METHOD, htu: requestURL,<br/>iat: epochSecond, ath: base64url(SHA-256(accessToken)) }
    KeyMgr->>KeyMgr: header = { typ: "dpop-proof", alg: "EdDSA", jwk: publicJwk }<br/>sign with privateKey (EdDSA)
    KeyMgr->>DB: updateLastUsed(keyId, now)
    KeyMgr-->>Filter: signed proof JWT

    Note over Client,DB: Step 3: Validation (DPoPService.validateProofForResource)

    Filter->>DPoP: validateProofForResource(proof, method, uri, token, keyId)
    DPoP->>DPoP: keyId + proof present?
    DPoP->>KeyMgr: getPublicKeyJwk(keyId)
    KeyMgr-->>DPoP: OKP public JWK
    DPoP->>DPoP: Jwks.parser().parse(jwk).toKey() -> PublicKey
    DPoP->>DPoP: Verify EdDSA signature over the proof
    DPoP->>DPoP: Reject unless header alg == "EdDSA"
    DPoP->>DPoP: htm equalsIgnoreCase request method
    DPoP->>DPoP: htu matches (scheme dropped, host + port + path compared)
    DPoP->>DPoP: abs(now - iat) <= 60_000 ms
    DPoP->>DPoP: purge expired jti entries, then putIfAbsent(keyId:jti)
    Note right of DPoP: Single-use per key id (RFC 9449 §11.1).<br/>A replay returns "jti already used (replay detected)".
    DPoP->>DPoP: ath == base64url(SHA-256(accessToken))
    DPoP->>KeyMgr: getPublicKeyThumbprint(keyId)
    KeyMgr-->>DPoP: thumbprint
    DPoP-->>Filter: DPoPValidationResult.valid(thumbprint)

    Note over Client,DB: Step 4: Binding checks and grant

    Filter->>Filter: JwtUtil.getDPoPThumbprint(accessToken) == proof thumbprint?
    Filter->>Filter: JwtUtil.getUserIdFromToken(accessToken) == dpop_keys.user_id?
    Filter->>Filter: set Authentication(userId, [DPOP_VERIFIED])
    Filter-->>Client: 200 OK + guild settings

    Note over Client,DB: Failure modes

    alt No / invalid / expired cookie
        Filter-->>Client: 401 { "error": "invalid_session", ... }
    else Access token expired or bad signature
        Filter-->>Client: 401 { "error": "invalid_session",<br/>"error_description": "Browser session token expired or invalid" }
    else Proof or binding check fails
        Filter-->>Client: 401 { "error": "invalid_session",<br/>"error_description": "DPoP session validation failed" }<br/>or "Token is not bound to this browser session"
    end

    Note over Client,DB: Stolen-cookie resistance

    Note over Client,DB: An attacker who copies the cookie ciphertext still cannot use it:<br/>the key id must resolve to an active row whose access token is DPoP-bound to the<br/>same Ed25519 key, and the cookie itself is authenticated AES-GCM.<br/>Session rotation (/api/session/rotate) issues a fresh key and retires the old one.

    Note over Client,DB: Revocation

    Client->>Filter: POST /api/auth/logout (cookie only)
    Filter->>KeyMgr: clearKeyPair(keyId)
    KeyMgr->>DB: UPDATE dpop_keys SET is_active = false
    Note right of DB: No tokenBindings map exists any more —<br/>revocation is the is_active flag on the key row.